## Backup & Recovery

### Backup Types

#### Logical Backup (Export/Import)
```bash
# Export data
expdp username/password@db DIRECTORY=dump_dir 
       DUMPFILE=backup.dmp LOGFILE=export.log

# Import data
impdp username/password@db DIRECTORY=dump_dir 
       DUMPFILE=backup.dmp LOGFILE=import.log
```

#### Physical Backup (RMAN)
```bash
# Connect to RMAN
rman target / catalog rman_catalog/password@db

# Backup database
BACKUP DATABASE;

# Backup with archive logs
BACKUP DATABASE PLUS ARCHIVELOG;

# Incremental backup
BACKUP INCREMENTAL LEVEL 1 DATABASE;

# List backups
LIST BACKUP;
```

### Recovery

#### Recover from RMAN Backup
```sql
-- Startup mount
STARTUP MOUNT;

-- Restore database
RMAN> RESTORE DATABASE;
RMAN> RECOVER DATABASE;

-- Open database
ALTER DATABASE OPEN RESETLOGS;
```

#### Recover Using Archive Logs
```sql
-- Mount database
STARTUP MOUNT;

-- Recover
RECOVER DATABASE USING BACKUP CONTROLFILE;

-- Or apply specific archive
RECOVER DATABASE USING BACKUP CONTROLFILE 
UNTIL CANCEL;
```

### Archive Logs
```sql
-- Enable archiving
SHUTDOWN IMMEDIATE;
STARTUP MOUNT;
