## Common Issues & Solutions

### Issue: ORA-00001 - Unique Constraint Violated
```sql
-- Cause: Attempt to insert duplicate value in unique column
-- Solution 1: Check existing values
SELECT COUNT(*) FROM employees WHERE emp_id = 100;

-- Solution 2: Use next sequence value
INSERT INTO employees (emp_id, emp_name) 
VALUES (emp_seq.NEXTVAL, 'John');

-- Solution 3: Handle in application
BEGIN
    INSERT INTO employees VALUES (100, 'John', 50000);
EXCEPTION
    WHEN DUP_VAL_ON_INDEX THEN
        UPDATE employees SET emp_name = 'John' WHERE emp_id = 100;
END;
```

### Issue: ORA-00904 - Invalid Column Name
```sql
-- Cause: Misspelled column or schema name
-- Solution 1: Check table structure
DESC employees;

-- Solution 2: Check user_tab_columns
SELECT column_name FROM user_tab_columns 
WHERE table_name = 'EMPLOYEES';

-- Solution 3: Verify column name spelling
SELECT emp_name, salary FROM employees;  -- Correct
SELECT emp_name, sal FROM employees;     -- Wrong - ORA-00904
```

### Issue: ORA-01830 - Date Format Error
```sql
-- Cause: Invalid date format in TO_DATE
-- Wrong
SELECT * FROM employees 
WHERE hire_date = TO_DATE('2025-01-01', 'DD-MON-YYYY');

-- Correct
SELECT * FROM employees 
WHERE hire_date = TO_DATE('01-JAN-2025', 'DD-MON-YYYY');
```

### Issue: ORA-12514 - TNS Could Not Resolve Service Name
```bash
# Cause: Database service not registered or not started
# Solution 1: Check service name in tnsnames.ora
# File location: $ORACLE_HOME/network/admin/tnsnames.ora

# Solution 2: Start database
STARTUP;

# Solution 3: Register service
lsnrctl reload

# Solution 4: Connect using direct path
sqlplus username/password@(DESCRIPTION=(ADDRESS_LIST=(ADDRESS=(PROTOCOL=TCP)(HOST=localhost)(PORT=1521)))(CONNECT_DATA=(SERVICE_NAME=orcl)))
```

### Issue: ORA-01555 - Snapshot Too Old
```sql
-- Cause: Long-running queries with UNDO tablespace issue
-- Solution 1: Increase UNDO retention
ALTER SYSTEM SET undo_retention=900;

-- Solution 2: Increase UNDO tablespace size
ALTER TABLESPACE undotbs1 ADD DATAFILE 
    '/u01/oradata/undotbs01_02.dbf' SIZE 500M;

-- Solution 3: Commit more frequently in loop
FOR i IN 1..1000000 LOOP
    -- Process record
    IF MOD(i, 1000) = 0 THEN
        COMMIT;
    END IF;
END LOOP;
```

### Issue: ORA-00060 - Deadlock Detected
```sql
-- Cause: Two transactions waiting for each other
-- Solution 1: Reduce lock time
BEGIN
    UPDATE accounts SET balance = balance - 100 WHERE acc_id = 1;
    UPDATE accounts SET balance = balance + 100 WHERE acc_id = 2;
    COMMIT;  -- Commit quickly
EXCEPTION
    WHEN OTHERS THEN
        ROLLBACK;
END;

-- Solution 2: Use consistent lock order
BEGIN
    UPDATE accounts SET balance = balance - 100 WHERE acc_id = 1;
    UPDATE accounts SET balance = balance + 100 WHERE acc_id = 2;
    COMMIT;
EXCEPTION
    WHEN OTHERS THEN
        ROLLBACK;
END;
```

### Issue: ORA-06502 - Numeric or Value Error
```sql
-- Cause: Value too large for NUMBER variable
-- Wrong
DECLARE
    v_num NUMBER(3);
BEGIN
    v_num := 9999;  -- Exceeds 3 digits
END;

-- Correct
DECLARE
    v_num NUMBER(5);
BEGIN
    v_num := 9999;
END;
```

