**Q2: What is the difference between Instance and Database?**

A: 
```
Instance:
- Memory structures (SGA - System Global Area, PGA - Program Global Area)
- Background processes (SMON, PMON, DBWn, LGWR, ARCH)
- Running processes and connections
- Can be started/stopped
- One database can have multiple instances (RAC)

Database:
- Physical files on disk (datafiles, control files, redo logs)
- Permanent storage
- One database = one set of physical files
- Cannot run without instance
```

Analogy: Instance is like the running software, Database is the persistent storage.

