Usage:
INSERT INTO employees (emp_id, emp_name)
VALUES (emp_seq.NEXTVAL, 'John Doe');

-- NEXTVAL: Get next value (increments)
-- CURRVAL: Get current value (no increment)

SELECT emp_seq.CURRVAL FROM dual;

Key Points:
- Sequence independent of table
- NEXTVAL always increments (gaps possible on rollback)
- CURRVAL returns last used value
- Commonly used for surrogate keys
- Multi-user safe (internal locking)

Example with DEFAULT:
CREATE TABLE employees (
    emp_id NUMBER DEFAULT emp_seq.NEXTVAL PRIMARY KEY,
    emp_name VARCHAR2(50)
);

INSERT INTO employees (emp_name) VALUES ('Jane Doe');
-- emp_id automatically filled
```

