**Q15: Explain the concept of NORMALIZATION.**

A:
```
Normalization: Organizing data to minimize redundancy

Benefits:
- Reduces data redundancy
- Improves data integrity
- Reduces storage space
- Improves query performance
- Easier maintenance

Drawbacks:
- More complex queries (more joins)
- Can reduce performance for reporting
- Requires careful design

Normal Forms:

1NF - Atomic values (no repeating groups)
BEFORE:
StudentID | Courses
1         | Math, Physics, Chemistry

AFTER:
StudentID | Course
1         | Math
1         | Physics
1         | Chemistry

2NF - No partial dependencies (remove columns dependent on part of PK)
BEFORE:
StudentID | CourseID | StudentName | CourseName
1         | C1       | John        | Math

AFTER:
Students:
StudentID | StudentName
1         | John

Courses:
CourseID | CourseName
C1       | Math

Enrollments:
StudentID | CourseID
1         | C1

3NF - No transitive dependencies (non-key columns don't depend on other non-key columns)
BEFORE:
StudentID | StudentName | DeptID | DeptName

AFTER:
Students:
StudentID | StudentName | DeptID

Departments:
DeptID | DeptName

Key Points:
- Most tables in 3NF
- BCNF rarely needed
- Denormalization for performance (carefully)
- Balance between normalization and query performance
