**Q18: Explain TRANSACTION ISOLATION LEVELS in detail.**

A:
```
Isolation Levels: Control transaction visibility

READ UNCOMMITTED (Lowest isolation)
- Can read uncommitted data (dirty read)
- Fastest performance
- Rarely used in production
- Example:
  Transaction 1: UPDATE account SET balance = 900 (not committed)
  Transaction 2: Can read balance = 900 (dirty)

READ COMMITTED (Oracle default)
- Cannot read uncommitted data
- Non-repeatable reads possible
- Good for most applications
- Example:
  Transaction 1: Read balance = 1000
  Transaction 2: Commits UPDATE balance = 900
  Transaction 1: Read balance = 900 (different)

REPEATABLE READ
- Cannot have non-repeatable reads
- Phantom reads possible
- Row-level consistency
- Example:
  Transaction 1: Read rows WHERE dept = 10 (5 rows)
  Transaction 2: Inserts new row WHERE dept = 10
  Transaction 1: Read same query (still 5 rows guaranteed)

SERIALIZABLE (Highest isolation)
- Highest isolation level
- Transactions execute serially
- Prevents phantom reads
- Slowest performance
- Example:
  Transaction 1: Read rows WHERE dept = 10
  Transaction 2: Cannot insert new row WHERE dept = 10

Problem Matrix:
┌──────────────┬──────────┬──────────────────┬──────────┐
│ Level        │ Dirty    │ Non-repeatable   │ Phantom  │
├──────────────┼──────────┼──────────────────┼──────────┤
│ Uncommitted  │ YES      │ YES              │ YES      │
│ Committed    │ NO       │ YES              │ YES      │
│ Repeatable   │ NO       │ NO               │ YES      │
│ Serializable │ NO       │ NO               │ NO       │
└──────────────┴──────────┴──────────────────┴──────────┘

Setting in Oracle:
SET TRANSACTION ISOLATION LEVEL SERIALIZABLE;
BEGIN
    -- Transaction code
    COMMIT;
END;
```

